text:
&gt; i stayed off lifting for 2 weeks so depressed and hurt when i bend forward, but when i trained again, the pain had gone away, but i avoided the compound lifts the "big three" as what they called. i still got big however, doing ppl program, training six days a week, tons of volume and did heavy weights on exercises that didn't strain my back (as far as i know).
&gt; 
&gt; 

which routine you followed?

i do the same and go 6 times a week to the gym. ofcourse my schedule is way differrent than most people but without those extra 30-40 mins of cardio i wouldnt be able to keep up my cardiovascular endurance and low percentage body fat. im 210 lbs shredded since the time i started. i used to be 150lbs 5.8ft.

&amp;#x200b;

keep it up its doing wonders to your physique and your mental health

gym anxiety for the first time this year fuck!

&amp;#x200b;

calmer now but had unbearable anxiety last week, last two times at the gym i was already on edge but had two men approach me both days in a row, and normally i would think nothing of it or even forget after a couple of hours but i already stressed and was put too much over the edge. kept up the gym habit to get rid of the stress too lmao

&amp;#x200b;

it is monday now and... i am nervous to go to the gym as if i am a beginner again. not horrific anxiety but i feel so uneasy and going to go at night hoping for fewer people. i am so nervous wtf i already often see the girl whose car i hit in the parking lot too...that is fine but i just want men to leave me alone. i look like a sweaty angry rat too so idk why it happened

thank you so much for the advice. i usually eat fairly healthy, lots of chicken ground beef, and some sausage, eggs, rice, noodles, potatoes, broccoli, and zucchini are all staples in my diet. i don't get as much fruit as i should but that's fairly easy to work on. so if i'm eating fairly healthy and i track my protein i probably shouldn't worry about calories right? i still might track just to be sure i'm on course but i'm not terribly worried about an eating disorder, i used to track calories when i was slimming down from being a bit chubby and i never had disordered eating. 

&amp;#x200b;

regarding having a good physique at my current weight, does this mean eating at maintenance and just working out a lot so that my fat is burned and that energy builds muscle? also is tdee calculators the best way to find maintenance?

&amp;#x200b;

it's good to hear that bike riding won't screw my recovery, because i love it. i know a lot of lifters dont do a lot of cardio so hopefully this will be helpful to me. 

&amp;#x200b;

thanks for the weight advice. it's hard to go with a low weight when everyone around you is lifting heavy but i don't want to injure myself so i will stick with what's safe.

&amp;#x200b;

thank you so much!
